From 6d263067e2d9a3fed65811e3593e9d101b9d823e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TofuJoe <darryl.hon@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 07:57:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 22/32] drm/xe/shrinker: Protect only idle active BOs, only
 from kswapd (review)

Follow-up to "Leave BOs of actively used VMs alone":

- GPU TT pages don't count in RSS, so a reclaimer that could not take
  active BOs might see the OOM killer pick a bystander. Only kswapd honours
  the protection now. Every other reclaimer (direct reclaim, drop_caches,
  memory.reclaim) runs with no_wait_gpu and skips BOs with unsignaled
  fences in ttm_bo_shrink_suitable(), so protect only BOs whose resv is
  idle: those stay reclaimable by direct reclaim, and busy ones stay
  reclaimable by kswapd, which waits for them. No BO is refused by every
  reclaimer. This replaces a time-based escape valve that reviews found
  too slow and racy.
- Don't protect LR VMs: their preempt fences never signal on their own,
  and they are restored by the rebind worker, not by exec.
- Stamp vm->last_exec_jiffies only after a job was pushed, not for failed
  or no-op execs.
- Only protect BOs bound in a VM (the ones an exec restores).
- Nothing is protected while system suspend or hibernation is prepared.
- Active skips return -EAGAIN and are bounded like -EBUSY skips; the
  256-skip bound now applies per memory type.
- Keep the xe_bo_shrink() kernel-doc adjacent to the function.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
